Subject: spi: designware: bound Rx transfers to the Rx FIFO depth

Tree: /mnt/2tb/unvr-port-refs/u-boot-v2026.07 (UBOOT_TREE)
Issue: #91

A polled consumer that falls behind overruns the Rx FIFO; the symptom is
the environment failing to load off SPI flash. Chunk the transfer to the
FIFO depth so the consumer cannot fall behind by more than one FIFO.

Currently invisible - uboot-port/drivers/spi/designware_spi.c is copied
over the upstream file wholesale.

diff --git a/drivers/spi/designware_spi.c b/drivers/spi/designware_spi.c
index b520c727..bb873043 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/designware_spi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/designware_spi.c
@@ -674,10 +674,30 @@ static int dw_spi_exec_op(struct spi_slave *slave, const struct spi_mem_op *op)
 	return ret;
 }
 
-/* The size of ctrl1 limits data transfers to 64K */
+/*
+ * CTRLR1 (NDF) is 16-bit, so any single transfer is limited to 64K.
+ *
+ * awto-unvr #91: additionally bound a *read* to the Rx FIFO depth. In
+ * EEPROM-read mode the controller free-runs all NDF frames into the Rx FIFO
+ * with no back-pressure; a slow polled consumer (e.g. per-byte log_content at
+ * LOGLEVEL 8) drains late, the FIFO overruns, and the read is silently
+ * corrupted ("FIFO overflow on Rx" -> env load fails -> default env). Capping a
+ * read at fifo_len means every frame the controller clocks in fits even if the
+ * CPU never reads until the end, so consumer speed can't overrun it - the
+ * spi-mem layer just issues more (address-advanced) reads. Writes stay at 64K:
+ * dw_writer()/tx_max() already flow-control Tx against the FIFO, so they can't
+ * overrun and shouldn't lose throughput. SPI here is env (64K) + MAC EEPROM
+ * only, so the extra read commands are immaterial to boot time.
+ */
 static int dw_spi_adjust_op_size(struct spi_slave *slave, struct spi_mem_op *op)
 {
-	op->data.nbytes = min(op->data.nbytes, (unsigned int)SZ_64K);
+	struct dw_spi_priv *priv = dev_get_priv(slave->dev->parent);
+
+	if (op->data.dir == SPI_MEM_DATA_IN && priv->fifo_len)
+		op->data.nbytes = min_t(unsigned int, op->data.nbytes,
+					priv->fifo_len);
+	else
+		op->data.nbytes = min(op->data.nbytes, (unsigned int)SZ_64K);
 
 	return 0;
 }
